From b3cd48fa34f02fe0fc8ebd3346e5f92fa5d3ec10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:29:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] rec-wasm: update the chain builder's self-loop comment

The comment still said every single-block self-loop emits the idle
fast-forward. Since the fast-forward predicate was narrowed only pure
polls and bare waits do. The chain builder keeps excluding every
self-loop on purpose, so the chain choice does not depend on that
predicate; the comment now says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MGX7KQ5gfrWApgW64pZbQ5
---
 core/rec-wasm/rec_wasm.cpp | 19 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/rec-wasm/rec_wasm.cpp b/core/rec-wasm/rec_wasm.cpp
index 87c41ba4c..7a6e75652 100644
--- a/core/rec-wasm/rec_wasm.cpp
+++ b/core/rec-wasm/rec_wasm.cpp
@@ -4586,14 +4586,17 @@ static std::vector<RuntimeBlockInfo*> discoverChain(RuntimeBlockInfo* entry) {
 	std::vector<RuntimeBlockInfo*> chain;
 	chain.push_back(entry);
 
-	// ★ IDLE-LOOP EXCLUSION (2026-07-17, chain-shadow finding): single-block
-	// modules emit the idle soft fast-forward (cap cycle_counter at 32) in
-	// their epilogue; buildMultiBlockModule does NOT. An idle link spinning
-	// in-module runs a different cc trajectory than the capped single block
-	// — the chain-shadow farm measured exactly this (304/6656 pc diffs,
-	// chain running further than the reference). Idle loops gain nothing
-	// from chaining (memory-bound waits); keep their verified single-block
-	// semantics by never chaining from or into them.
+	// SELF-LOOP EXCLUSION (2026-07-17 chain-shadow finding, comment updated
+	// 2026-11-02): a single-block module emits the idle soft fast-forward (cap
+	// cycle_counter at 32) in its epilogue only when fly_block_idle_ff accepts
+	// the block (a pure poll or a bare wait, no memory writes, no loop-carried
+	// registers); buildMultiBlockModule never emits it. An accepted loop
+	// spinning in-module would run a different cc trajectory than the capped
+	// single block (the chain-shadow farm measured 304/6656 pc diffs, chain
+	// running further than the reference). This test is deliberately wider
+	// than fly_block_idle_ff: it excludes EVERY self-loop, including counted
+	// delays that run at full cost, so the chain/no-chain choice never depends
+	// on the fast-forward predicate. Self-loops gain nothing from chaining.
 	auto fly_is_idle = [](RuntimeBlockInfo* blk) {
 		u32 c = BET_GET_CLS(blk->BlockType);
 		if (c == BET_CLS_Static && blk->BlockType != BET_StaticIntr
